version: 1.0.0
description: AI-native animation engine — declarative YAML format (.atelier files) authored through MCP tools, rendered to Canvas 2D/SVG, exported to video/Lottie
context:
  - 'Monorepo: 11 packages (types, math, schema, core, canvas, svg, lottie, react, studio, mcp, cli) + 2 apps (playground, showcase)'
  - 'Build order: types + math (parallel) → schema → core → canvas → svg + lottie + react + studio + mcp + cli (parallel)'
  - 'Primary AI interface: @atelier/mcp exposes 52 tools across 16 tool groups for structured animation authoring'
  - 27 animatable properties, 5 easing types, state machines (hierarchical + transitions), templates, presets, assets, variables, interactions, refs
  - Blend modes (16 Canvas 2D composite operations), motion path animation, clip paths, gradient animation, audio sync
  - 'Export paths: browser (WebCodecs MP4/WebM/GIF via studio), CLI (FFmpeg MP4/GIF), SVG string, Lottie JSON, React component'
features:
  animation-engine:
    description: Core animation pipeline — define layers, states, and deltas as YAML; resolve any frame via interpolation and easing; hierarchical states with parent inheritance; smooth state transition interpolation
    components:
      - '#atelier-types'
      - '#atelier-math'
      - '#atelier-schema'
      - '#atelier-core'
  rendering:
    description: Canvas 2D renderer — shapes, text, images, groups, gradients, shadows, stroke trim, blend modes, motion paths, clip paths
    components:
      - '#atelier-canvas'
  svg-renderer:
    description: SVG renderer — render any frame as an SVG string for thumbnails, SSR, and static export
    components:
      - '#atelier-svg'
  lottie-export:
    description: Lottie JSON exporter — lossy but best-effort conversion of .atelier documents to Lottie format
    components:
      - '#atelier-lottie'
  react-integration:
    description: React integration — Animation component, useAnimation hook, useAnimationState hook for embedding Atelier in React apps
    components:
      - '#atelier-react'
  ai-authoring:
    description: MCP server with 52 tools across 16 groups for AI agents to create, edit, preview, export, and analyze animations
    components:
      - '#atelier-mcp'
  studio:
    description: Browser editor widget — canvas preview, YAML viewer, GUI editor, undo/redo, drag-to-reorder, MP4/WebM/GIF export
    components:
      - '#atelier-studio'
  cli:
    description: Command-line tool — validate, info, still, render, export-svg, export-lottie, assets, variables (9 commands)
    components:
      - '#atelier-cli'
components:
  atelier-types:
    description: 60+ TypeScript type definitions across 16 modules — layers, deltas, easing, states, shadows, audio, assets, variables, interactions, presets
    file: packages/types/src/index.ts
  atelier-math:
    description: Pure interpolation engine — easing functions, spring physics, color lerp, path interpolation
    file: packages/math/src/index.ts
  atelier-schema:
    description: Zod validation schemas + YAML parse/serialize with AI-readable errors
    file: packages/schema/src/index.ts
  atelier-core:
    description: Animation engine — resolveFrame, DocumentBuilder, StateMachine (hierarchical + transitions), blendResolvedFrames, templates, presets, expression evaluator, audio timing, unit resolver
    file: packages/core/src/index.ts
  atelier-canvas:
    description: Canvas 2D renderer — renderFrame, shapes, text, images, gradients, shadows, stroke trim
    file: packages/canvas/src/index.ts
  atelier-svg:
    description: SVG renderer — renderFrameSVG, shape/gradient/filter/clip/text mapping to SVG elements
    file: packages/svg/src/index.ts
  atelier-lottie:
    description: Lottie JSON exporter — exportToLottie, layer/shape/keyframe/easing/color mapping with unsupported feature warnings
    file: packages/lottie/src/index.ts
  atelier-react:
    description: React integration — Animation component, useAnimation/useAnimationState hooks, AnimationPlayer class
    file: packages/react/src/index.ts
  atelier-studio:
    description: Browser editor widget + video/GIF export via WebCodecs + easing curve editor with interactive bezier control points
    file: packages/studio/src/index.ts
  atelier-mcp:
    description: MCP server — 61 tools across 15 groups for AI animation authoring (document, layer, state, delta, visual, asset, variable, preset, template, interaction, ref, audio, overlay, recipe, import)
    file: packages/mcp/src/index.ts
  atelier-cli:
    description: CLI tool — validate/lint, the video pipeline (trim, transcribe, transcript, captions), recipes (recipe, apply-recipe), rendering (still, render, export-svg/lottie/image, carousel), assets/variables, and the studio editor
    file: packages/cli/src/index.ts
aspects:
  layer-tag-isolation:
    description: Every content pipeline owns a layer tag-namespace (silence-trim, caption, caption-word, overlay) and on re-run drops ONLY its own tagged layers before re-adding them — never touching user-authored (untagged) layers or other pipelines' outputs. The load-bearing invariant that lets AI regenerate content repeatedly without erasing human work or sibling pipeline output.
    tags:
      - convention
      - pipeline
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/cli/src/lib/video-project.ts:319
      - packages/cli/src/lib/caption-builder.ts:93
      - packages/cli/src/lib/recipe.ts:334
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:143
    enforcement: filter-by-tag before rewrite
  detected-vs-user-edited:
    description: AI-detected content (silence-cut boundaries, transcript words) is immutable, but user overrides — padding, userEdited/userAdded/hidden flags, corrected text — are preserved across re-runs by matching fresh detections to existing entries on timing tolerance plus unchanged detected text. Fix a misheard word or nudge a cut, re-run the pipeline, and the human edit survives.
    tags:
      - convention
      - pipeline
      - core-invariant
    anchors:
      - packages/cli/src/lib/cut-model.ts:127-139
      - packages/cli/src/lib/transcript-model.ts:109-124
    enforcement: merge-on-match (timing tolerance + unchanged detected text)
  copy-on-write-doc:
    description: Any code that mutates an AtelierDocument constructs a NEW document object (spread the doc, replace the layers/assets arrays) before calling DocumentStore.set — it never mutates the stored object in place. Guarantees a concurrent reader (notably the live WebSocket bridge broadcasting to the studio) can never observe a half-mutated document mid-update.
    tags:
      - convention
      - immutability
      - concurrency
    anchors:
      - packages/cli/src/lib/video-project.ts:349
      - packages/cli/src/lib/caption-builder.ts:118-121
      - packages/cli/src/lib/recipe.ts:359-362
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/import-images.ts:179
      - packages/mcp/src/tools/recipes.ts:169
    enforcement: build-new-doc-before-set
  source-tagged-mutation:
    description: DocumentStore mutations carry a source tag (human | llm | system). The studio WebSocket bridge re-broadcasts a change to the browser ONLY when source is llm; human-sourced changes (the browser is already current) and system-sourced changes (file-read hydration) stay silent. Prevents echo loops and false "agent edited" attribution on the live human↔LLM editing loop.
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:17
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:62-65
      - packages/mcp/src/store.ts:114-127
      - packages/cli/src/commands/studio.ts:280-289
      - packages/cli/src/commands/studio.ts:2789-2807
      - packages/studio/src/studio.ts:237-312
    tags:
      - convention
      - live-bridge
      - attribution
    enforcement: source-filtered broadcast
  types-schema-duplication:
    description: Type definitions are the source of truth for the document shape, but several closed unions (notably AnimatableProperty, ~35 members) are DUPLICATED in @atelier/schema's Zod schemas — adding an animatable property or visual type requires editing BOTH packages or validation silently rejects it.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - source-of-truth
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/types/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: keep types and schema unions in sync
  math-pure-deterministic:
    description: Every export is a pure function — no state, no IO, no clock, no RNG. This is what lets resolveFrame (which composes these) stay deterministic and reproducible across seek, export, and SSR.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - determinism
      - pure-function
    anchors:
      - packages/math/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: pure functions only
  schema-validation-boundary:
    description: The single validation boundary — every .atelier document crossing from text/agent into the engine validates here, returning flat AI-readable path+message errors. parseAtelier never throws (try/catch into a ValidationResult).
    tags:
      - package-level
      - boundary
      - validation
    anchors:
      - packages/schema/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: validate-at-boundary
  core-engine-no-rendering:
    description: The engine resolves frames and runs state machines but performs NO rendering or IO — output is a plain ResolvedFrame consumed by the separate renderer packages (canvas/svg/lottie). resolveFrame is pure; adding a renderer never touches core.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - architecture
      - separation
    anchors:
      - packages/core/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: engine emits data, renderers consume
  canvas-renderer-no-dom:
    description: Renders a ResolvedFrame against a minimal RenderContext interface (not DOM CanvasRenderingContext2D), so the same code drives browser canvas, OffscreenCanvas, and node/@napi-rs backends with no DOM-lib dependency.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - portability
      - renderer
    anchors:
      - packages/canvas/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: depend on RenderContext interface only
  svg-declarative-emit:
    description: Emits SVG markup as STRINGS (declarative) rather than imperative ctx calls; some canvas features are lossy here (e.g. combined shadow+tint drops the tint). Output is self-contained with a <defs> block for gradients/clips.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - renderer
      - lossy
    anchors:
      - packages/svg/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: string emission with self-contained defs
  lottie-lossy-subset:
    description: Exports a SUBSET of Atelier features to Lottie JSON; unsupported features (audio, expressions, shadow, motion path, clip path, multi-state) are reported through the warnings catalog rather than silently dropped.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - export
      - lossy
    anchors:
      - packages/lottie/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: warn on unsupported, never silently drop
  react-imperative-via-ref:
    description: The animation player is driven imperatively through a ref (play/pause/seek); the document is deliberately NOT render-triggering state, and the rAF loop is torn down on unmount to prevent leaks.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - lifecycle
      - integration
    anchors:
      - packages/react/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: ref-driven player + unmount teardown
  studio-embeddable-widget:
    description: A framework-agnostic editor widget — host apps embed AtelierStudio, observe edits via onDocumentChange, and push external edits via applyMutation (suppress-notify to avoid echo). The CLI's `atelier studio` is just one host.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - widget
      - embeddable
    anchors:
      - packages/studio/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: embeddable widget with callback + applyMutation
  mcp-shared-store-multi-transport:
    description: '61 tools over a SINGLE shared DocumentStore, reachable via stdio (Claude Desktop) and WebSocket (the studio bridge) at once; mutations flow through one onChange emitter. Gotcha: most tools mutate in place without store.set, so onChange fires only for the few that do.'
    tags:
      - package-level
      - architecture
      - gotcha
    anchors:
      - packages/mcp/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: one store, multiple transports
  cli-thin-over-engine:
    description: Commands are thin orchestrators over the engine packages — parsing, IO, and flag-handling only, with no animation logic of their own. The same npm package ships both the `atelier` CLI and the `atelier-mcp` server bins.
    tags:
      - package-level
      - architecture
      - thin-layer
    anchors:
      - packages/cli/src/index.ts:1
    enforcement: orchestrate engine packages, no domain logic
